    "content": "NASA leads the Artemis program, but the spacecraft and rockets are built by major aerospace contractors: Lockheed Martin builds the Orion crew capsule, Boeing produces the Space Launch System (SLS) core stage, and Northrop Grumman manufactures the solid rocket boosters. Airbus provides the European Service Module. Key Contractors & Roles: Orion Spacecraft (Capsule): Built by Lockheed Martin. European Service Module (ESM): Built by Airbus. Space Launch System (SLS) Rocket Core Stage: Built by Boeing. SLS Solid Rocket Boosters: Built by Northrop Grumman. Interim Cryogenic Propulsion Stage (ICPS): Built by United Launch Alliance (a Boeing/Lockheed Martin joint venture). Engines (RS-25): Produced by Aerojet Rocketdyne. These major partners, along with hundreds of subcontractors, are building the hardware for NASA's return to the Moon, with missions currently operating in 2026.",
